# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets out of it.
#
# This file is not an optimisation. `.env` holds a real DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET
# and Supabase service-role key. Every COPY in the Dockerfile is explicit today,
# so none of them would copy .env into a layer - but a build context is uploaded
# to the daemon in full, and a future `COPY . .` would silently bake the secrets
# into an image that gets pushed to a registry. Denying them here means that
# mistake is impossible rather than merely unlikely.

# --- secrets: never let these enter the build context ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# --- local infrastructure and data ---
# The isolated Postgres cluster and the portable Redis live here. ~60MB, and it
# is a live database - it has no business in an image.
pgdata/
redis/
log/
start-pg.cmd
start-redis.cmd
bootstrap-db.sql

# --- python ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- tests: not needed to serve traffic ---
tests/
# The suite pins a separate database and asserts on internals; shipping it just
# makes the image larger and invites running it against production by accident.

# --- editors / os ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.git/
.gitattributes
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- docs ---
*.md
!../README.md
